BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy Workshop for Teens: Tracking Sunspots
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T180000
UID:6a48118886636e3d00527f5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program begins with a short lesson on sunspots—what the
 y are\, why they form\, and how they tell us about solar activity. Partici
 pants will then use a Seestar telescope to take their own live pictures of
  the Sun and identify sunspots in the photos/videos. The Seestar app will 
 be used to connect to the telescope. If the weather is cloudy\, we will in
 stead work with today’s real-time solar image from NASA’s Solar Dynami
 cs Observatory. Participants can compare their images with archival ones t
 o track sunspot movement and changes over time. A portion of the event wil
 l take place outdoors weather permitting.\nThis program is part of Youth H
 ub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in
  the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious
  snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call th
 e branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a48118886636e3d00527f5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
