UID:6a67d7be0d65ac360042a54e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Orange Shirt Day and National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
  are observed annually on September 30. In this workshop\, Brianna Patrick
 \, Objiway beading artist\, will explain the significance of Orange Shirt 
 Day and guide participants in the creation of individual Orange Shirt Day 
 pins that raise awareness and recognize the historical and ongoing trauma 
 that Indigenous peoples experience as a result of the residential school s
 ystem. Presenter will be virtual\, but program is in person.\nThis program
  is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens 
 after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available.
