BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Summer Workshop for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260814T140000
UID:6a15f4f8278f7c2f008fc3c8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Canadian Training Institute is thrilled to present a two-p
 art series that will introduce participants to wellness practices that can
  be utilized in their everyday lives to enhance their state of well-being.
  Topics will include:\nStress management and the art of de-stressing\nSelf
 -awareness\nMindfulness and Meditation\nVolunteer hours can be provided to
  participants upon completion of the camp.\nPlease note that this program 
 is for teens ages 13-17 only.
LOCATION:Beaches
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a15f4f8278f7c2f008fc3c8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Tiramisu Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T170000
UID:6a3d56410e851028002d22b7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of how to make the classic Italian dessert\, 
 Tiramisu. Chef Yumiko will provide and explain all the ingredients and tak
 e the participants through a simple step-by-step process of creating a del
 icious ready-to-eat dish.\nFood allergy notice\n: Please be aware that ing
 redients used in this program include dairy\, egg and decaffeinated espres
 so. Certain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people.\
 nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pla
 ce for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alwa
 ys available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bran
 ch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Woodside Square
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d56410e851028002d22b7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Quick Chaotic Board Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T170000
UID:69deafe2c1cf6f9a75855cca@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come play fun and quick chaotic board games such as Spaceteam\
 , Dutch Blitz\, and Ghost Blitz! If you’ve never played these games befo
 re\, don’t worry. The Youth Hub Librarian will go over the rules at the 
 beginning of each game. You’ll be a pro at each game before you know it!
 \nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pl
 ace for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alw
 ays available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bra
 nch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Youth Hub or Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69deafe2c1cf6f9a75855cca
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Disassemble a Computer Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T153000
UID:6a41712fed35742f00fefce5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what's going on inside a computer? Ever
  wanted to take apart a computer to see? This workshop is your chance!\nFr
 ee Geek Toronto is a non-profit organization dedicated to getting unwanted
  computers and electronics back into working condition. During this worksh
 op\, we'll go over what's inside a computer\, how to properly open a deskt
 op\, and safety guidelines to follow when it comes to working with electro
 nics.\nRegistration is required.\nRegistration begins on Monday\, July 27.
 \nPlease register at the branch or by calling 416-393-7700. Space is limit
 ed. For teens aged 13 to 19.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Main Street\, Basement Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a41712fed35742f00fefce5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Interview Skills 4 Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T140000
UID:6a42b5de4407827f8aa82f01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Increase your potential for success and learn how to   ace tho
 se interviews! This program will introduce skills such   as speaking profe
 ssionally\, what kind of questions to expect\, interview   processes\, pre
 paration and learning to exude genuine   confidence.\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a42b5de4407827f8aa82f01
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Bars & Beats
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T173000
UID:6a43eb1e4447d04586320276@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop led by Coach Desiree McKenzie\, participants 
 will explore the global and local roots of spoken word\, specifically exam
 ining how rap music utilizes poetic tools like rhythm\, metaphor\, and sto
 rytelling.\nThe goal of this program is to help participants recognize rap
  as poetry in motion\, examine lyrics analytically\, and create original s
 poken word pieces inspired by musical flow and technique.\nNo registration
  is required. Drop-in only.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Yo
 uth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, 
 where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are of
 fered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to fi
 nd out more.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a43eb1e4447d04586320276
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
